00:08:06,457 --> 00:08:07,825
BECAUSE, YOU KNOW,
I AM GETTING OLDER.

238
00:08:07,825 --> 00:08:08,860
AND I'M GONNA GET FATTER.

239
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:10,461
CAN'T TOUCH THAT NET.

240
00:08:10,461 --> 00:08:11,396
BUT I REALLY DON'T THINK
THIS WAS THE WAY

241
00:08:11,396 --> 00:08:12,397
TO GO ABOUT IT.

242
00:08:12,397 --> 00:08:13,498
COME ON NOW!

243
00:08:13,498 --> 00:08:14,566
KEEP YOUR HEAD DOWN.

244
00:08:14,566 --> 00:08:18,570
BRE, GO.

245
00:08:18,570 --> 00:08:20,505
MY BRA IS RUINED.

246
00:08:20,505 --> 00:08:22,373
KIM, GO.

247
00:08:22,373 --> 00:08:24,442
YEAH, KIM.

248
00:08:24,442 --> 00:08:26,578
OKAY, KYLE, GO!

249
00:08:26,578 --> 00:08:27,879
KEEP YOUR BUTT DOWN.

250
00:08:27,879 --> 00:08:29,714
AND ON YOUR BACK.

251
00:08:29,714 --> 00:08:31,316
JUST KEEP GOING.

252
00:08:31,316 --> 00:08:32,450
I CAN FEEL IT GOING DOWN
MY PANTS.

253
00:08:32,450 --> 00:08:33,851
AND I CAN FEEL IT IN MY EARS.

254
00:08:33,851 --> 00:08:35,453
YOU CAN DO IT, KYLE! COME ON!

255
00:08:35,453 --> 00:08:37,288
AND I CAN FEEL MY HAIR.

256
00:08:37,288 --> 00:08:38,923
OH, IT'S JUST--
IT'S A GROSS FEELING.

257
00:08:38,923 --> 00:08:40,792
EW, IT'S IN MY EAR.

258
00:08:40,792 --> 00:08:43,394
KYLE, ONE COULD SAY
THAT SHE WASN'T AS INTO IT

259
00:08:43,394 --> 00:08:44,829
AS EVERYBODY ELSE WAS.

260
00:08:44,829 --> 00:08:46,231
GOOD LUCK, NICOLE.

261
00:08:46,231 --> 00:08:46,898
ALL RIGHT, A HEART FOR YOU.

262
00:08:46,898 --> 00:08:47,899
GO, NICOLE!

263
00:08:47,899 --> 00:08:49,234
THERE YOU GO!

264
00:08:49,234 --> 00:08:50,268
CRANK IT UP, NICOLE.

265
00:08:50,268 --> 00:08:51,469
COME ON, PUSH THROUGH IT.

266
00:08:51,469 --> 00:08:53,238
PUSH THROUGH IT.

267
00:08:53,238 --> 00:08:54,439
COME ON!

268
00:08:54,439 --> 00:08:56,841
AH.

269
00:08:56,841 --> 00:08:58,243
LET'S GO, NICOLE.

270
00:08:58,243 --> 00:09:00,445
NICOLE, SHE DID NOT HAVE FUN.

271
00:09:00,445 --> 00:09:03,848
JUST THE COMPLAINTS IN GENERAL,
A LOT OF LIKE, "OH, MY GODS."

272
00:09:03,848 --> 00:09:04,849
I'M GONNA BARF.

273
00:09:04,849 --> 00:09:06,618
THAT WAS SO NASTY.

274
00:09:06,618 --> 00:09:09,854
NIK, GO.

275
00:09:09,854 --> 00:09:11,723
YOU ARE DOING GREAT.

276
00:09:11,723 --> 00:09:13,625
GO, GO, GO.

277
00:09:13,625 --> 00:09:14,759
WHOO!

278
00:09:14,759 --> 00:09:19,864
GO, GO, GO, GO.

279
00:09:19,864 --> 00:09:22,800
I THINK NIK HANDLED
THE SITUATION PRETTY WELL...

280
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,603
WITH HER PANTS PRACTICALLY
AT HER ANKLES.

281
00:09:25,603 --> 00:09:29,507
DOWN, DOWN!

282
00:09:29,507 --> 00:09:30,875
THERE YOU GO.

283
00:09:30,875 --> 00:09:32,543
DON'T TOUCH THAT NET.

284
00:09:32,543 --> 00:09:34,679
GOOD.

285
00:09:34,679 --> 00:09:35,747
ALL RIGHT, HERE WE GO.

286
00:09:35,747 --> 00:09:36,914
LET'S GO. LET'S GO!

287
00:09:36,914 --> 00:09:38,449
GIRL, YOU'RE ALMOST HOME FREE!

288
00:09:38,449 --> 00:09:39,651
ACTUALLY, THAT WAS FUNNY.

289
00:09:39,651 --> 00:09:41,552
AND IT WAS A FREEING FEELING.

290
00:09:41,552 --> 00:09:43,488
I KNOW IT WAS TOUGH
WHEN YOU GOT DIRTY.

291
00:09:43,488 --> 00:09:45,256
BUT YOU GUYS DID FANTASTIC.

292
00:09:45,256 --> 00:09:48,459
NOW,
I DO HAVE SOMETHING FOR YOU.

293
00:09:48,459 --> 00:09:50,295
"YOU'RE DIRTY. YOU'RE GRIMY
YOU'RE STINKY. YOU'RE SMELLY.

294
00:09:50,295 --> 00:09:52,930
SO TODAY YOU'RE GONNA HAVE TO
FAKE THE FUNK. TYRA."

295
00:09:52,930 --> 00:09:53,931
WHAT THE HELL DOES THAT MEAN?

296
00:09:53,931 --> 00:09:54,732
WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

297
00:09:54,732 --> 00:09:55,933
WE DON'T KNOW.

298
00:09:55,933 --> 00:09:57,969
DOING A PHOTO SHOOT
LIKE THIS.

299
00:09:57,969 --> 00:10:00,204
I DON'T ENJOY BEING COVERED
IN DIRT AND GRIME.

300
00:10:00,204 --> 00:10:02,607
HOWEVER, IF IT'S GONNA GET ME
CLOSER TO THE TOP,

301
00:10:02,607 --> 00:10:05,510
I GUESS IT'S ALL WORTH IT.

302
00:10:11,616 --> 00:10:14,686
OH, THIS IS SO SAD.

303
00:10:14,686 --> 00:10:16,754
I FELT LIKE
I WAS GONNA THROW UP.

304
00:10:16,754 --> 00:10:18,423
I'M NOT LIKE,
I WASN'T EVEN LIKE

305
00:10:18,423 --> 00:10:19,490
EXAGGERATING.

306
00:10:19,490 --> 00:10:20,792
THIS IS NUTS.

307
00:10:20,792 --> 00:10:22,593
PEOPLE CAN'T SIT AROUND
AND BE DIRTY ALL DAY.

308
00:10:22,593 --> 00:10:24,562
I FEEL LIKE A CAGED RAT.

309
00:10:24,562 --> 00:10:25,797
OH, GROSS.

310
00:10:25,797 --> 00:10:27,699
BEING COVERED
IN ALL THAT STUFF--

311
00:10:27,699 --> 00:10:29,300
IT'S JUST ABSOLUTELY DISGUSTING.

312
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:32,203
MY HAIR WAS--
IT LOOKED LIKE A COW PIE.

313
00:10:32,203 --> 00:10:33,571
WHAT DID THE TYRA MAIL SAY?

314
00:10:33,571 --> 00:10:35,306
FAKE THE FUNK.

315
00:10:35,306 --> 00:10:36,841
YEAH, FAKE THE FUNK.

316
00:10:36,841 --> 00:10:38,710
SO WE HAVE TO FAKE
THE NASTY SMELL.

317
00:10:38,710 --> 00:10:40,211
OH, BELIEVE ME,
I DON'T HAVE TO FAKE THE FUNK.

318
00:10:40,211 --> 00:10:42,780
YOU CAN'T MOVE
BECAUSE YOU'RE WET AND SLIMY.

319
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:45,316
AND WE PULL UP TO THIS LOFT
IN L.A.

320
00:10:45,316 --> 00:10:48,219
WE'RE CLUELESS
ON WHAT'S GOING ON.

321
00:10:51,923 --> 00:10:53,324
HI.

322
00:10:53,324 --> 00:10:54,926
I AM BRANDON HOLLEY.
I'M FROM "ELLE GIRL."

323
00:10:54,926 --> 00:10:56,494
I'M THE EDITOR.

324
00:10:56,494 --> 00:10:59,630
THIS IS MARIE, OUR ART DIRECTOR,
AND GLORIA, OUR FASHION EDITOR.

325
00:10:59,630 --> 00:11:02,667
SO HOW DO YOU FEEL RIGHT NOW?
YOU'RE ON A GO-SEE.

326
00:11:02,667 --> 00:11:04,669
THE WINNER OF
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"

327
00:11:04,669 --> 00:11:06,671
WILL ALSO BE ON THE COVER
OF "ELLE GIRL."

328
00:11:06,671 --> 00:11:08,673
AND EVEN THOUGH
YOU'RE COVERED IN MUD,

329
00:11:08,673 --> 00:11:10,375
YOU HAVE TO LET
YOUR NATURAL PERSONALITY

330
00:11:10,375 --> 00:11:11,776
SHINE THROUGH.

331
00:11:11,776 --> 00:11:12,977
ARE YOU NERVOUS?

332
00:11:12,977 --> 00:11:14,846
OR IS THE MUD MAKING YOU--
HOW DO YOU FEEL?

333
00:11:14,846 --> 00:11:16,447
JUST GOTTA GO IN AND JUST
SHOW MY PERSONALITY.

334
00:11:16,447 --> 00:11:17,949
'CAUSE YOU'RE DEFINITELY
NOT GONNA GO

335
00:11:17,949 --> 00:11:18,282
ON THESE LOOKS RIGHT NOW.

336
00:11:18,282 --> 00:11:21,452
WHAT CAN MY READER
SEE IN YOU THAT'S DIFFERENT?

337
00:11:21,452 --> 00:11:23,454
IN MY PICTURES
I LIKE TO SHOW LIKE

338
00:11:23,454 --> 00:11:24,589
A LOT OF CONFIDENCE.

339
00:11:24,589 --> 00:11:26,457
SOMETHING LIKE,
"YEAH, YOU WANT TO READ THIS,

340
00:11:26,457 --> 00:11:27,458
UH-HUH."

341
00:11:27,458 --> 00:11:29,460
WHAT DO YOU THINK
YOU COULD BRING

342
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:31,295
TO AN "ELLE GIRL" COVER?

343
00:11:31,295 --> 00:11:32,797
LOOKING AT ALL THESE COVERS,
THEY ALL HAVE THE SAME

344
00:11:32,797 --> 00:11:34,599
FACIAL EXPRESSION, SAME SMILE.

345
00:11:34,599 --> 00:11:36,200
MY SMILE WOULD BE BIG.

346
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:37,535
BE LIKE THIS...

347
00:11:37,535 --> 00:11:40,471
ONE OF MY MOTTOS IS
"DARE TO BE DIFFERENT."

348
00:11:40,471 --> 00:11:42,707
TELL US
HOW YOU DARE TO BE DIFFERENT?

349
00:11:42,707 --> 00:11:44,475
I KINDA LIKE TO HAVE FUN,
BUT I HAVE FUN IN WEIRD WAYS.

350
00:11:44,475 --> 00:11:45,810
LIKE WHAT?

351
00:11:45,810 --> 00:11:47,478
LIKE PLAYING IN THE MUD
IS ACTUALLY FUN.

352
00:11:47,478 --> 00:11:48,780
I DON'T KNOW.

353
00:11:48,780 --> 00:11:50,648
I'M JUST ONE OF THOSE TYPES
OF PEOPLE WHO LIKES

354
00:11:50,648 --> 00:11:51,649
TO GET INTO THINGS
AND MESS THINGS UP.

355
00:11:51,649 --> 00:11:52,917
WHAT MAKES YOU DIFFERENT?

356
00:11:52,917 --> 00:11:54,252
MY TASTE IN MUSIC IS
IS DEFINITELY DIFFERENT

357
00:11:54,252 --> 00:11:55,553
THAN EVERYONE ELSE'S.

358
00:11:55,553 --> 00:11:56,888
WHICH IT IS?

359
00:11:56,888 --> 00:11:58,956
I LISTEN TO LIKE
ELECTROCLASH, PSYCHOBILLY,

360
00:11:58,956 --> 00:12:00,291
HARDCORE.

361
00:12:00,291 --> 00:12:02,393
YOU KNOW WHAT,
THAT'S VERY "ELLE GIRL."

362
00:12:02,393 --> 00:12:04,228
AFTER ROLLING THE MUD ALL DAY,
HOW DO YOU FEEL?

363
00:12:04,228 --> 00:12:05,830
WELL, AT FIRST--
I FEEL OKAY NOW.

364
00:12:05,830 --> 00:12:08,466
BUT THE MUD
WAS A LITTLE SMELLY.

365
00:12:08,466 --> 00:12:10,635
I'M SURPRISED THAT "ELLE GIRL"
WANTED TO TALK

366
00:12:10,635 --> 00:12:12,537
TO OUR SMELLY BUTTS.

367
00:12:12,537 --> 00:12:13,704
WHO WOULD WANNA TALK
TO SOMEONE WHO HAS

368
00:12:13,704 --> 00:12:15,540
ROLLED AROUND IN POOP?

369
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:17,375
SO WHEN WE WERE ROLLING
THROUGH THE MUD, I WAS LIKE,

370
00:12:17,375 --> 00:12:18,910
"UGH"
I ALMOST PUKED.

371
00:12:18,910 --> 00:12:20,611
WHAT CAN YOU TELL OUR READERS
ABOUT YOURSELF?

372
00:12:20,611 --> 00:12:22,280
WELL, I'M FROM
A REALLY SMALL TOWN.

373
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,815
YOU KNOW,
I WORK AT THE LOCAL DAIRY QUEEN.

374
00:12:23,815 --> 00:12:25,883
I'M JUST, YOU KNOW,
THE LOCAL SMALL-TOWN GIRL.

375
00:12:25,883 --> 00:12:27,485
DO YOU HAVE ANY PASSION?

376
00:12:27,485 --> 00:12:28,686
I LOVE JEWELRY.

377
00:12:28,686 --> 00:12:30,288
JEWELRY IS MY MAIN THING.

378
00:12:30,288 --> 00:12:31,689
LIKE I HAVE SO MANY EARRINGS.

379
00:12:31,689 --> 00:12:32,857
EARRINGS ARE MY PASSION.

380
00:12:32,857 --> 00:12:33,958
I WAS MYSELF.

381
00:12:33,958 --> 00:12:34,959
I WAS JUST NATURAL.

382
00:12:34,959 --> 00:12:35,960
I WASN'T NERVOUS AT ALL.

383
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:38,362
BUT, UM, HOPEFULLY,
IT'S MY THIRD WIN.

384
00:12:38,362 --> 00:12:39,964
MY STYLE IS LIKE
THE WAY THAT I EXPRESS MYSELF.

385
00:12:39,964 --> 00:12:41,966
AND LIKE
MY SEXUALITY AND EVERYTHING,

386
00:12:41,966 --> 00:12:43,901
IT'S LIKE
THE MOST IMPORTANT THING

387
00:12:43,901 --> 00:12:45,303
ABOUT MY OUTWARD APPEARANCE.

388
00:12:45,303 --> 00:12:47,305
WHAT IF WE PUT YOU
IN A SUPER FRILLY

389
00:12:47,305 --> 00:12:48,306
GIRLIE-GIRL DRESS?

390
00:12:48,306 --> 00:12:49,640
NO, I MEAN,
THAT'S A GREAT QUESTION.

391
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,342
ONE OF THE MAIN ASPECTS OF
OF BEING A MODEL

392
00:12:51,342 --> 00:12:52,643
IS BEING REALLY VERSATILE.

393
00:12:52,643 --> 00:12:53,444
WE'RE GONNA TAKE
SOME POLAROID'S OF YOU.

394
00:12:53,444 --> 00:12:55,313
THE DIRT'S A GREAT ACCESSORY.

395
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:03,788
MY PUNK FACE.

396
00:13:04,922 --> 00:13:07,658
MORE ENERGY.

397
00:13:07,658 --> 00:13:08,793
HI.

398
00:13:08,793 --> 00:13:10,728
THIS HAS BEEN GREAT FOR US.

399
00:13:10,728 --> 00:13:14,565
BECAUSE EACH OF YOU WAS ABLE TO
SHOW US A BIT ABOUT YOURSELF.

400
00:13:14,565 --> 00:13:17,768
SO THE WINNER OF THIS CHALLENGE
IS GOING TO RECEIVE SOMETHING

401
00:13:17,768 --> 00:13:20,738
REALLY AWESOME--
A ONE-ON-ONE LESSON

402
00:13:20,738 --> 00:13:24,408
FROM A FASHION INDUSTRY EXPERT
ON HOW TO BE A REAL MODEL.

403
00:13:24,408 --> 00:13:26,444
AND ONLY ONE OF YOU WILL WIN.

404
00:13:26,444 --> 00:13:28,279
WHAT WE'RE GONNA DO IS
GO DOWN AND TELL YOU EACH

405
00:13:28,279 --> 00:13:30,281
WHAT WE THOUGHT OF YOU.

406
00:13:30,281 --> 00:13:32,216
LISA, YOU HAD GREAT ENERGY
FROM THE SECOND YOU WALKED

407
00:13:32,216 --> 00:13:33,384
IN THE ROOM.

408
00:13:33,384 --> 00:13:36,454
JAYLA, YOU SEEMED REALLY SHY
AND LIKE YOU WERE

409
00:13:36,454 --> 00:13:37,855
UNDER A LOT OF STRESS
AND ABOUT TO CRACK.

410
00:13:37,855 --> 00:13:40,258
I'M COVERED IN MUD,
AND I'M GOING ON A GO-SEE.

411
00:13:40,258 --> 00:13:42,260
YOU CAN'T LET PEOPLE KNOW
WHEN YOU FEEL UNCOMFORTABLE.

412
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:44,962
BRE, I THINK
YOU SHOWED A LOT OF CONFIDENCE,

413
00:13:44,962 --> 00:13:47,198
BUT THAT'S SOMETHING
THAT DIDN'T ALWAYS COME

414
00:13:47,198 --> 00:13:48,566
ACROSS IN THE POLAROIDS.

415
00:13:48,566 --> 00:13:50,801
NIK, MY ONE CRITIQUE WOULD BE
THAT YOU NEED

416
00:13:50,801 --> 00:13:51,936
A LITTLE MORE ENERGY.

417
00:13:51,936 --> 00:13:54,205
NICOLE, YOU JUST HAVE
THIS LIKE

418
00:13:54,205 --> 00:13:56,207
AMERICA'S SWEETHEART THING
GOING ON.

419
00:13:56,207 --> 00:13:58,209
AND THAT'S DEFINITELY
A TYPE OF LOOK

420
00:13:58,209 --> 00:14:00,211
THAT PEOPLE ARE, YOU KNOW,
INTERESTED IN.

421
00:14:00,211 --> 00:14:01,779
KIM, YOU'RE TOUGH,
AND YOU'VE GOT YOUR OWN THING.

422
00:14:01,779 --> 00:14:03,481
AND I LOVE IT.

423
00:14:03,481 --> 00:14:06,284
BUT YOU'VE GOTTA BE ABLE
TO CHANGE IT UP A LITTLE BIT.

424
00:14:06,284 --> 00:14:07,919
KYLE, I LOVE THAT YOU WORKED
AT DAIRY QUEEN.

425
00:14:07,919 --> 00:14:08,920
THAT'S SO AWESOME.

426
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:09,921
YEAH.

427
00:14:09,921 --> 00:14:11,355
YOU'RE REALLY SUPER STRIKING.

428
00:14:11,355 --> 00:14:12,657
YOU'VE GOT GREAT BONE STRUCTURE.

429
00:14:12,657 --> 00:14:14,692
YOU'RE COMFORTABLE
IN FRONT OF THE CAMERA.

430
00:14:14,692 --> 00:14:17,395
MAYBE YOU NEED TO WORK ON
A RANGE OF EXPRESSIONS.

431
00:14:17,395 --> 00:14:19,797
NOW THAT WE'VE MET
ALL OF YOU,

432
00:14:19,797 --> 00:14:22,266
WE'VE COME TO A DECISION.

433
00:14:22,266 --> 00:14:24,669
SO THE ONE THAT WE PICKED
UM, WAS LISA.

434
00:14:24,669 --> 00:14:26,671
YOU'RE THE WINNER
OF THE CHALLENGE.

435
00:14:26,671 --> 00:14:28,706
WHAT YOU'RE GETTING
IS A REALLY COOL

436
00:14:28,706 --> 00:14:30,975
FASHION CRASH COURSE.

437
00:14:30,975 --> 00:14:33,311
THEY TOLD ME THEY THOUGHT
THAT I WAS FANTASTIC.

438
00:14:33,311 --> 00:14:35,947
HOWEVER, AS USUAL,
MY POSING WASN'T PERFECT

439
00:14:35,947 --> 00:14:38,916
IN THE PICTURES,
SO THEY CHOSE LISA.

440
00:14:38,916 --> 00:14:40,618
I PERSONALLY THINK
SHE'S THE LEAST PRETTY

441
00:14:40,618 --> 00:14:41,919
OF EVERYONE HERE.

442
00:14:41,919 --> 00:14:43,220
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

443
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:44,322
DO YOU GUYS WANT HUGS?

444
00:14:44,322 --> 00:14:45,690
NO, THANK YOU.

445
00:14:49,961 --> 00:14:53,264
NO,
I CALLED THE SHOWER SECOND!

446
00:14:53,264 --> 00:14:56,267
YOU CAN TAKE THAT ONE.

447
00:14:56,267 --> 00:14:57,868
PLEASE HURRY UP
WITH THE SHOWERS, YOU GUYS.

448
00:14:57,868 --> 00:15:00,504
OVERALL,
THE DAY IS KIND OF DEPRESSING.

449
00:15:00,504 --> 00:15:02,673
I'M JUST REALLY UPSET
WITH MYSELF THAT I DIDN'T DO

450
00:15:02,673 --> 00:15:04,208
AS WELL AS I'D PLANNED.

451
00:15:06,477 --> 00:15:08,913
I JUST WON THE CHALLENGE
WHERE I GET TO LEARN A BUNCH OF

452
00:15:08,913 --> 00:15:11,582
THINGS FROM A FASHION EXPERT.

453
00:15:11,582 --> 00:15:14,552
AND I AM SO EXCITED.

454
00:15:14,552 --> 00:15:15,553
HELLO.

455
00:15:15,553 --> 00:15:17,888
HELLO, I'M TODD HALLMAN.

456
00:15:17,888 --> 00:15:18,956
HELLO. LISA.

457
00:15:18,956 --> 00:15:21,492
CELEBRITY STYLIST,
FASHION RUNWAY PRODUCER.

458
00:15:21,492 --> 00:15:22,760
COME.

459
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,328
I'M HERE TO GIVE YOU AN EDGE.

460
00:15:24,328 --> 00:15:25,429
SO WE'LL GET IN SOME CLOTHES.

461
00:15:25,429 --> 00:15:26,797
WE'LL WALK.

462
00:15:26,797 --> 00:15:28,633
WE'LL SEE
WHAT WE HAVE TO WORK WITH.

463
00:15:28,633 --> 00:15:30,635
JAYLA,
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU DIDN'T

464
00:15:30,635 --> 00:15:32,570
TAKE A SHOWER
AND YOU'RE SITTING ON THE BED,

465
00:15:32,570 --> 00:15:33,437
I PUT A TOWEL DOWN.

466
00:15:33,437 --> 00:15:34,639
GROSS.

467
00:15:34,639 --> 00:15:36,307
THAT'S DISGUSTING, DUDE.

468
00:15:36,307 --> 00:15:38,576
TAKE A SHOWER
BEFORE YOU SIT ON A BED.

469
00:15:38,576 --> 00:15:40,578
KIM'S REALLY SARCASTIC
ABOUT THINGS.

470
00:15:40,578 --> 00:15:42,546
UM, I DON'T THINK
THAT SHE FEELS

471
00:15:42,546 --> 00:15:43,948
THAT SHE'S DOING TOO WELL.

472
